        return template.replace("Hello World", sanitize(user_input))
</code></pre>
<h2 id="solution">Solution</h2>
<p>The solution is to use the regular expression library <code>re</code> to match and replace the user input in the template.</p>
<pre class="language-python"><code>import re

def sanitize(input):
    return input.replace("&lt;", "{{").replace("&gt;", "}}")

class ClassX:
    def render(self, template, user_input):
        return re.sub("Hello World", sanitize(user_input), template)
</code></pre>
<p>The regular expression <code>Hello World</code> is used to match the user input. The user input is sanitized before replacing it with the template.</p>
<h2 id="notes">Notes</h2>
<ul>
<li><code>re.sub()</code> is used to replace the user input in the template with the sanitized user input.</li>
