#### The `if` statement
This is a control flow statement which will check if the condition is `true` or `false`.

```java
if (condition) {
    // Do some code
}
```

#### The `switch` statement
This is a control flow statement which will check what value the variable is and then execute the code that corresponds to that value.

```java
switch (variable) {
    case 1:
        // Do some code
        break;
    case 2:
        // Do some code
        break;
    case 3:
        // Do some code
        break;
    case 4:
        // Do some code
        break;
    default:
        // Do some code
}
```

#### The `for` loop
This is a control flow statement which will execute the code in the loop as long as the condition is `true`.

```java
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    // Do some code
}
```

#### The `while` loop
This is a control flow statement which will execute the code in the loop as long as the condition is `true`.

```java
while (condition) {
    // Do some code
}
```

#### The `do-while` loop
This is a control flow statement which will execute the code in the loop as long as the condition is `true`.

```java
do {
    // Do some code
} while (condition);
```

#### The `break` keyword
This is a control flow statement which will stop the code from executing any further.

```java
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    if (i == 5) {
        break;
    }
    // Do

}
